Worldwide subject to the following Geographic Areas Exclusion Clause LSW617J (Amended):

1. Notwithstanding any provision to the contrary within this insurance it is agreed that this insurance excludes any loss, damage, cost or expense of whatsoever nature directly or indirectly caused by, resulting from or in connection with any of the following regardless of any other cause or event contributing concurrently or in any other sequence to the loss:
(a) war, invasion, acts of foreign enemies, hostilities or warlike operations whether war be declared or not;
(b) civil war, revolution, rebellion, insurrection, civil commotion assuming the proportions of or amounting to an uprising, military or usurped power;
(c) confiscation, nationalisation, seizure, detention, appropriation, requisition for title or use by or under the order of any government whether civil, military or de facto;
(d) Cuba, Iran, North Korea, Syria, the Crimea region of Ukraine, and the Donetsk and Luhansk regions of Ukraine;
(e) Venezuela.

2. However coverage pursuant to this Policy is granted:
(a) overflight of and technical stops in territories listed in 1 above provided no passengers embark or disembark and no cargo loaded or discharged;
(b) in the event of force majeure.

3. Any excluded country may be covered by underwriters' individual agreement if required and subject to an additional premium, terms and conditions as underwriters may decide.

